v 3
d importR: import R data files (.Rdata, .Rda, .Rds) into Stata over an R or Python bridge
d
d .Rdata and .Rds files are compressed binary objects in R's own serialization
d format, so there is no pure-Stata way to read them; something outside Stata has
d to do the decoding.  importR takes a dual-bridge approach so that it works on
d machines with R and on machines without it.  It first looks for Rscript and, if
d found, converts the file through the haven package.  If R is absent it falls
d back to Stata's built-in Python integration and the pyreadstat library.  Either
d path lands the data in memory; the choice is reported so you know which bridge
d ran.  Handles .Rdata, .Rda, and .Rds.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer, plus ONE of:
d   R with the haven package (Rscript on the PATH), or
d   Stata's Python integration with pyreadstat (python pip install pyreadstat).
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260725
d
